.DS_Store

# ── Obsidian ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore vault config by default, then un-ignore the files that make a fresh
# clone reproducible. community-plugins.json and appearance.json are here
# deliberately: without them a clone gets every plugin's code and Obsidian
# enables none of it, and the theme selection is lost. That was the single
# biggest reproducibility gap in the workspace this template came from.
**/.obsidian/*
!**/.obsidian/plugins/
!**/.obsidian/themes/
!**/.obsidian/bases/
!**/.obsidian/snippets/
!**/.obsidian/app.json
!**/.obsidian/appearance.json
!**/.obsidian/community-plugins.json
!**/.obsidian/core-plugins.json
!**/.obsidian/graph.json
!**/.obsidian/hotkeys.json
!**/.obsidian/templates.json
!**/.obsidian/daily-notes.json

# Per-machine plugin state. Each machine writes its own from the .example file
# beside it, via `./workspace obsidian-setup`. See each plugin's SETUP.md.
#   icloud-sync      data.json holds an absolute icloudBasePath.
#   agentic-copilot  data.json is a local preference file, and editApprovalMode
#                    is a security choice that should not arrive from a clone.
# Excalidraw needs no line here. It is store-installed, so the whole plugin is
# ignored below. It would have needed one otherwise: its data.json is ~57%
# personal stencil library and pen presets, rewritten every session, and a
# single-line 171 KB JSON blob that git cannot merge.
.obsidian/plugins/icloud-sync/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/agentic-copilot/data.json

# Store-installed plugins, listed by id to match .obsidian/plugins/store-plugins.json.
# Four of the five are GPL-3.0 or AGPL-3.0, so a `git add -A` after installing
# them from Obsidian's browser would commit copyleft binaries into an MIT tree,
# which is the exact thing not vendoring them exists to prevent. Ids rather than
# a blanket rule, so the two vendored plugins stay tracked and the
# obsidian-plugin-missing gate can still tell "expected from the store" apart
# from "enables a plugin that is nowhere".
.obsidian/plugins/templater-obsidian/
.obsidian/plugins/notebook-navigator/
.obsidian/plugins/table-editor-obsidian/
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-excalidraw-plugin/
.obsidian/plugins/tag-wrangler/

# Themes are store-installed too. appearance.json carries the selection, which
# is the part that has to travel; the CSS itself is a two-click download.
.obsidian/themes/

# Per-machine pane layout. Also leaks the working set via lastOpenFiles.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# ── Vault boundary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This vault is a knowledge layer. Binaries and legal originals live in their
# own folders outside it and are referenced by relative path, never absorbed.
# See Standards/external-paths.md. Attachments/ holds only images the notes
# themselves produce (Excalidraw exports, screenshots).
#
# This is what makes the boundary a build failure rather than a norm: copying a
# signed PDF in does not produce a quiet 2 MB commit, it produces a file git
# refuses to stage.
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx
**/*.xlsx
**/*.pptx
**/*.sketch

# ── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commit only the scaffold: folder structure, .example templates, READMEs. A
# fresh clone gets a ready-to-fill skeleton and never a secret.
.credentials/**
!.credentials/**/
!.credentials/README.md
!.credentials/**/*.example
!.credentials/**/README.md
!.credentials/**/.gitkeep

# ── Harness runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.scratchpad/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv-*/
**/renderer/dist/
